# Copy to .env. Every npm script loads it.
#
# The workshop drives TWO different endpoints, and on a self-hosted setup they
# are not the same machine:
#
#   * the CONTROL PLANE  — create-slides.ts: agents, environments, sessions,
#     the SSE event stream, the Files API.
#   * the JUDGE endpoint — eval-runner.ts: the Messages API, with vision and a
#     structured result per slide.
#
# Against Anthropic's hosted API both are api.anthropic.com and you only need
# the first line. Against a self-hosted control plane they must be split: a
# wire-compatible Managed Agents deployment serves /v1/sessions but NOT
# /v1/messages, so the judges have to point at a real model endpoint.

# ── 1. Control plane ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Hosted Anthropic: an sk-ant-… key, and leave ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL unset.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...

# Self-hosted (e.g. managed-agent-platform's docker-compose stack). The key is
# that deployment's CONTROLPLANE_API_KEY.
# ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8080

# Resource ids, minted by `ant beta:environments create` / `ant beta:agents
# create`. Setting them here overrides the constants in src/create-slides.ts,
# which is handy when the same checkout drives two different deployments.
# ENVIRONMENT_ID=env_...
# AGENT_ID=agent_...

# Where to link session traces. {session} and {workspace} are substituted.
# Default is Anthropic's Console; managed-agent-platform's bundled console is:
# SESSION_URL_TEMPLATE=http://localhost:3000/sessions/{session}

# Self-hosted only. A wire-compatible deployment may harvest
# /mnt/session/outputs/ into the Files API *only* during an outcome grading
# cycle — with no outcome defined the deck is written in the sandbox and never
# indexed, so create-slides finds nothing to download. Set this to 1 to attach
# a minimal outcome to every session purely to trigger that harvest.
# HARVEST_VIA_OUTCOME=1

# ── 2. Judge endpoint ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Unset, the judges talk to api.anthropic.com with ANTHROPIC_API_KEY and the
# workshop behaves exactly as it always has. Point these at any endpoint that
# speaks Anthropic Messages when the control plane above cannot serve them.
# JUDGE_BASE_URL=https://api.anthropic.com
# JUDGE_API_KEY=sk-ant-...

# The judging model. It must accept image input — every aesthetic judge sends a
# rendered slide as a JPG.
# JUDGE_MODEL=claude-opus-4-7

# Anthropic's structured outputs (output_config) are a hosted-API feature. An
# endpoint that silently ignores them returns prose instead of a score, which
# scores the deck as NaN rather than failing. Set this to 1 to have the judges
# ask for the same schema through a forced tool call, which any Anthropic-
# protocol endpoint supports.
# JUDGE_VIA_TOOL_CALL=1
